From 707f06837a4b77d681a2bf6cbaea2bfeecdcb90f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:24:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: adoptedStyleSheets is an observable array

The adoptedStyleSheets getter returned a frozen array, so the common
pattern shadowRoot.adoptedStyleSheets.push(sheet) threw "can't define
array index property past the end of an array with non-writable length",
while Chrome accepts it since the attribute is an ObservableArray.

The bindings generator has no ObservableArray support, so Document and
ShadowRoot now hand out one cached proxy over a plain backing array. Its
set, defineProperty and deleteProperty traps validate indexed and length
changes like the WebIDL observable array handler, adopt the resulting list
through the existing set_adopted_stylesheet, and only then mirror it into
the backing array; every other trap forwards to the array, so
Array.isArray and the Array.prototype methods keep working. Assigning the
attribute now updates the same array object, as the spec requires.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
